KZ3 patch 2071 (RSX pass 67): the shared pipeline template, the RE notes "Pass 67".
A template is a list of pipeline records of hashes and numeric state only (libs/video/rsx_pso_template.h): FNV /
structural hashes and fingerprints of the vertex and fragment programs, the variant state words (texture-unit masks,
sRGB, vertex layout), the render state and the pipeline key. No shader text, microcode, address or string derived from
game data, so it can be shared.
1. Export: LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_OUT=<file> writes a record for every pipeline key the walker looks up (once per key), every
   5 s when it grew and at exit.
2. Prewarm: LD_PSO_TEMPLATE=<file> starts a scout thread that searches the running guest's committed memory for the
   programs the template lists (16-byte aligned, fingerprint of the first 16 bytes, then a full hash check); when a
   record's vertex and fragment program are both found, worker threads (LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_THREADS, 3) translate them with
   the walker's own translator, compile (shader disk cache first), create the pipeline through the pipeline library and
   stage it like a preloaded one. The walker merges staged pipelines at its next lookup; a pipeline that is not ready
   is built by the walker as before (no draw is skipped).
3. get_pso's translation step is now one function, ld_xlate (under a lock: the decompilers keep static scratch), shared
   by the walker and the prewarm; the walker's output is unchanged.
Merge tool: tools/smoke/pso_template.py; host test tools/smoke/test_pso_template.sh.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ld_xlate/ld_pso_key_tail (2071's shared translator) take upstream's VP branch bits (new ld_xl_in.vp_branch_bits, set_branch_bits in ld_xlate, hashed when the VP uses them; prewarm passes 0) and unnorm_dim[16][3] (records keep [16][2]; key hashes w,h only as before).

